# Secrets — never commit
.env

# Client workbooks — a customer's priced schedule and their running-account
# position. Commercial data; it does not belong in a history that gets cloned.
# The app never reads them at runtime; only tools/gen_demo_data.py and the
# importer tests do, and those skip when the file is absent.
# See fixtures/README.md for where to place them.
sify_boq.xlsx
annexure.xlsx
fixtures/*.xlsx

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Database dumps — confidential, and large
backups/

# Timestamped editor backups — `ABOUT.md.bak.20260809-1305`, `ra.py.bak.…-corr`.
# They were untracked but NOT ignored, so every `git status` listed twenty of
# them and a `git add -A` would have committed the lot. Git history is the
# revert point; these are not.
*.bak
*.bak.*

Quote.html
# Client source documents — the batch Manas collected for the Phase 3 / §8
# evidence pass: BOQs, RA bills, quotations, measurement sheets, a delivery
# challan, an attendance sheet. Real rates and real customers' details; they
# are read once for structure and never at runtime. SOURCE_DOCUMENTS.md is the
# findings record and IS tracked — the documents themselves are not.
client_docs/
